{
  "version": 1,
  "milestone": "M2",
  "format": {
    "summary": "Input for the seeded floor generator (GDD 5.15). Numbers (chances, counts, widths) live in balance.json under generator.* and world.*; this file holds shapes, pools and text only.",
    "slots": "A room of N modules has 2N floor slots and 2N wall slots, named floor0..floor(2N-1) and wall0..wall(2N-1), numbered outward from the room's door side. A slot's distance from the unit's front door edge is d = (first module index of the room * 240) + 240 * floor(k/2) + (k even ? 72 : 168), using balance.world.moduleWidthPx and slotOffsetsPx. World x: left wing x = 1440 - d, right wing x = 1680 + d. This keeps every same-layer pair >= 96 px apart and every slot >= 72 px from any doorway (min 48, world.doorwayClearancePx), because doorways are only at multiples of 240 from the front door.",
    "generationOrder": "Forced wings first: floor 15 left = your_flat, floor 13 Mara's flat, floor 14 bag flat (chosen from its template list in floorOverrides). Then roll the other wing by template weight, honouring balance generator.maxSameTemplatePerFloor, floorOverrides excludeTemplates and the flat-wing guarantee.",
    "unitModules": "Every template's room modules sum to balance.world.modulesPerWing (6). Front door is at d = 0.",
    "roomTypes.always": "Objects placed before pool fill. {object, layer, count?} puts count (default 1) in random free slots of that layer. {object, layer, slots:'all'} fills every slot of the layer. {oneOf:[{object,weight}], layer} picks one by weight. Pool fill then visits each remaining slot with chance generator.slotFillChance and a weighted pick from that layer's pool.",
    "roomTypes.pools": "Per layer: [{object, weight, max?}]. max = most copies per unit (not per room); copies placed by 'always' count toward max. When a max is used up, remove it from the pool for the rest of the unit and keep the other weights.",
    "templates.rooms": "[{ref, type, modules, position?}] position 'first' or 'last' pins the room to the front-door end or the far end; others are shuffled between them. adjacent: [[refA, refB]] means those rooms must be neighbours. Room instance ids use the room's final index: f<floor><L|R>-<roomIndex>-<slot>, e.g. f14R-2-wall1.",
    "templates.allowedConditions": "Conditions the generator may roll for this unit (conditions themselves: balance.generator.conditions). The start flat is normal only; offices and service units are never burned.",
    "templates.lootBias": "Optional map of item id to a weight multiplier applied to every loot table roll made inside the unit (elderly flat favours medicine, tins, seeds).",
    "templates.roomOverrides": "Optional per room ref: replaces 'always' entries of that room type (elderly bathroom always has a medicine cabinet).",
    "authored": "Only your_flat. A fully fixed layout: authored.doorsAfterRoom lists rooms followed by an interior door at their far boundary; objects list {object, layer, slot, fixedLoot?, rolls?, foundNote?}. Nothing is randomised, no pools are used, no zombies. 'workbench' is a fixture (GDD 5.15 Generator edge rules), not a salvage object.",
    "fixedLoot": "As in floors.json: [{id, qty}] guaranteed on first search. With fixedLoot the container makes 0 table rolls unless 'rolls' [min,max] is given. fixedLoot ignores the condition's emptyChance and is never removed or charred by a condition.",
    "guarantees": "Applied after filling and after conditions (GDD 5.15 steps 8-9). Each guaranteed object is exempt from ransack removal, charring and emptiness.",
    "zombies": "Crawler/walker choice uses balance generator.zombieTypeWeights. Room zombieWeight (0 = never) weights which room gets a zombie; counts, group chance, per-room cap and the 'not in the first module' rule come from balance.generator.",
    "notes": "notes[] are found notes (GDD 5.16). Each id is used at most once per game. containers lists the object ids that may hold it; unitTypes limits by unit type (flat, office, service). Pick 1-2 per floor (notesPerFloor) in a container that exists; a note is delivered on first search even if the container has no other loot."
  },
  "notesPerFloor": [1, 2],
